==Latin==
{{wikipedia|lang=la}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*speḱ-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro||*haru-speks}}, from {{m|itc-pro|*speks}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=haruspex, -icis|page=280}}</ref> The first component is related to {{m|la|hīra}}; the second is from the root of {{m|la|speciō||to observe, watch}}.<ref>{{R:Nocentini|hw=aruspice}}</ref> Compare {{cog|xfa|𐌇𐌀𐌓𐌉𐌔𐌐(𐌄𐌗)}}.

{{root|la|ine-pro|*ǵʰerH-|id=bowels}}
According to Nocentini<ref>{{R:Nocentini|hw=aruspice}}</ref> the first part stems from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ǵʰerH-||intestine|id=bowels}} (thus ''*ǵʰr̥H-u-'' > ''*xaru-''), whence also Latin {{m|la|hariolus}}, {{m|la|hernia||hernia}}.

Cognate to Ancient Greek {{m|grc|χορδή}}, Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*garnō||intestines}} (whence German {{m|de|Garn}}) and to Lithuanian {{m|lt|žarnà||intestine}}. The component {{m|la||-spex}} can also be found in the word {{m|la|auspex}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|haruspex}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|haruspex<3>|g=m}}

# [[diviner]] who reads from the intestines of sacrificial animals; one who practices [[haruspicy]].

